    "intro_html":  "Rendang is Indonesian beef cooked in coconut milk until the liquid disappears entirely and what is left clings to the meat like a dark, fragrant paste. It is not a curry you eat with a spoon. It is beef that has absorbed everything in the pot. That dryness is also why it is one of the best meal prep dishes there is, because there is no sauce to separate or go watery by Thursday. Each serving carries 836 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e38 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.28 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
